  {
    "field_name": "Validation Objective",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validates rocSOLVER dense LU TFLOPS, time-to-solution, and Residual Check: PASSED"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Execution Details and Purpose",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Build and run local bin/rochpl under mpirun --allow-run-as-root for yaml warmup plus timed repeats, parse GFLOPS, time-to-solution, and Residual Check, and abort if Residual Check is not PASSED, to measure sustained FP64 dense LU. Clamp problem_size_N from >=65536 to 32768"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run local FP64 rocSOLVER dense LU (mpirun bin/rochpl) with yaml problem_size_N (smoke 4096, baseline/extended 32768; >=65536 clamped to 32768) on one GPU (rocSOLVER chooses its own blocking), repeat solves per timed_repeats, then parse Final Score GFLOPS, time-to-solution, and Residual Check"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Builds local bin/rochpl (rocSOLVER dense LU) with a hipcc GCC pin, then runs mpirun --allow-run-as-root -np 1 bin/rochpl --N. problem_size_N >=65536 is clamped to 32768. num_iterations is capped by timed_repeats (6 at N>=32768 baseline, 16 extended). Residual Check: PASSED is required. The binary is single-GPU rocSOLVER dgetrf and dgetrs at one N; rocSOLVER picks its own block size and factorization, so there is no num_gpus, process grid, block_size or panel_factorization parameter. output_format: csv"
  },
